@HostAddress = http://localhost:5180

### 1. Health Check
# Checks service liveness. Returns 200 OK with status "Healthy".
GET {{HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Retrieve All Documents (GET)
# Retrieves all stored document metadata records ordered by newest first.
GET {{HostAddress}}/documents
Accept: application/json

### 3. Retrieve Single Document by ID (GET)
# Retrieves metadata for an individual document by its unique repository ID (e.g. doc-1).
GET {{HostAddress}}/documents/doc-1
Accept: application/json

### 4. Create Document via JSON Payload (POST)
# Creates a new text document and uploads the generated stream into Amazon S3.
POST {{HostAddress}}/documents
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "API Documentation Scratchpad",
  "description": "Created via .http scratchpad to test JSON POST route.",
  "fileName": "api-scratchpad.txt",
  "contentType": "text/plain",
  "content": "This document was generated using Wp1Fall26Aws.Api.http."
}

### 5. Upload Document via Multipart Form (POST)
# Uploads a binary/text file directly using multipart/form-data.
POST {{HostAddress}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Multipart Upload Demo
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Demonstrating multipart file persistence to AWS S3.
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="demo-upload.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is sample uploaded file content for AWS S3 document store.
--WebAppBoundary--

### 6. Update Document Metadata (PUT)
# Modifies the Title and Description of an existing document record.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/documents/doc-1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Project Specification v2",
  "description": "Updated architecture notes with comprehensive AWS S3 documentation."
}

### 7. Delete Document (DELETE)
# Removes a document record from the storage repository.
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/documents/doc-2
Accept: application/json

